{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"5834f08538bd19d0","name":"card_event_machines_of_war","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Soviet/WorldAtWar/events/card_event_machines_of_war","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"MACHINES OF WAR","text":"Add the top Soviet infantry unit in your deck to your support line.","flavorText":"During the opening stages of the German invasion of the Soviet Union the Red Army faced a serious shortage of weapons. The course of the war went on in such a way that most of the available munitions were lost, along with its troops who were either killed or captured, destroyed during a retreat or captured by the enemy in warehouses. The development and manufacturing of munitions in the Soviet Union had begun before the invasion, but in 1941 they stepped up their game and most of their weapon production was done during the invasion, in some cases under siege and isolation. From 1941 to 1945, the Soviet Union managed to produce over 30 million rifles and submachine guns, 1,476 million machine guns, 516,648 artillery guns, 347,900 mortars, 119,769 tanks and self-propelled guns, 265,600 army trucks, 213,742 military aircraft, 2 cruisers, 25 destroyers and 52 submarines.","faction":"Soviet","type":"order","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":5,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_machines_of_war","title":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_event_machines_of_war_title","SourceString":"MACHINES OF WAR","LocalizedString":"MACHINES OF WAR"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Soviet","kredits":5,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_event_machines_of_war_text","SourceString":"Add the top Soviet infantry unit in your deck to your support line.","LocalizedString":"Add the top Soviet infantry unit in your deck to your support line."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_event_machines_of_war_history","SourceString":"During the opening stages of the German invasion of the Soviet Union the Red Army faced a serious shortage of weapons. The course of the war went on in such a way that most of the available munitions were lost, along with its troops who were either killed or captured, destroyed during a retreat or captured by the enemy in warehouses. The development and manufacturing of munitions in the Soviet Union had begun before the invasion, but in 1941 they stepped up their game and most of their weapon production was done during the invasion, in some cases under siege and isolation. From 1941 to 1945, the Soviet Union managed to produce over 30 million rifles and submachine guns, 1,476 million machine guns, 516,648 artillery guns, 347,900 mortars, 119,769 tanks and self-propelled guns, 265,600 army trucks, 213,742 military aircraft, 2 cruisers, 25 destroyers and 52 submarines.","LocalizedString":"During the opening stages of the German invasion of the Soviet Union the Red Army faced a serious shortage of weapons. The course of the war went on in such a way that most of the available munitions were lost, along with its troops who were either killed or captured, destroyed during a retreat or captured by the enemy in warehouses. The development and manufacturing of munitions in the Soviet Union had begun before the invasion, but in 1941 they stepped up their game and most of their weapon production was done during the invasion, in some cases under siege and isolation. From 1941 to 1945, the Soviet Union managed to produce over 30 million rifles and submachine guns, 1,476 million machine guns, 516,648 artillery guns, 347,900 mortars, 119,769 tanks and self-propelled guns, 265,600 army trucks, 213,742 military aircraft, 2 cruisers, 25 destroyers and 52 submarines."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::WorldAtWar","isReserved":true,"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'Patriotic_Push'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Misc/OrdersFeb17/Patriotic_Push.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/G